From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi 939: keep the per-link identity across the mlsta band enrichment

nl80211 already returns correct per-link data for an MLO client.
nlwifi_get_mlsta_info_cb() (modules/nl80211/nlwifi.c:3482-3531) walks
NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINKS and fills, per link, the real mlo_link_id, the affiliated
client address and the link BSSID. iface_get_mlsta_info() then improves it once
more, joining on link id to write the affiliated AP BSSID
(modules/default/wifi.c:1950).

The very next line throws all of it away:

	ret = iface_get_sta_info_band(ifname, aplinks[j].band, macaddr, sta);

That helper is handed the MLD netdev and the MLD address of the client and has
no per-link concept. get_ctrl_interface_band() (wifi.c:1206) ignores its band
argument and returns the MLD ifname, so all three links talk to the same
hostapd socket; nlwifi_get_station_cb() then writes mlo_link_id =
WIFI_MLO_INVALID_LINK_ID (nlwifi.c:3204), macaddr = the MLD address and bssid =
if_gethwaddr(MLD netdev) (nlwifi.c:3224-3225); and hostapd_cli_get_sta_mlo()
(wpactrl/hostapd_ctrl.c:880-898) cannot repair any of it because it looks for
mlo_link_id=, mlo_bssid= and mlo_sta_link_addr=, none of which this hostapd
emits - it emits peer_addr[N]= instead. Storing -1 into a uint8_t is where the
255 comes from.

Patch 937 is what made this bite. Before it the hostapd enrichment ran only
where nl80211 had failed; 937 made it unconditional - correctly, because on
mt76 a GET_STATION dump on the MLD netdev returns nothing for an MLO client and
gating on it discarded good data. The cost is that the enrichment now lands on
every link of the mlsta path too, where nl80211 had in fact succeeded.

Measured on hardware 2026-08-02, one MLO client on ap-mld-1:

	ubus call wifi.apmld.ap-mld-1 stations
	  mlo_links[0]: link_id 255, link_bssid 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e, band 2.4GHz
	  mlo_links[1]: link_id 255, link_bssid 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e, band 6GHz

	real affiliated BSSIDs: link0 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e
	                        link1 7a:04:1c:81:9c:2e
	                        link2 76:04:1c:81:bc:2e

band is the one field that survives, because iface_get_sta_info_band() sets it
from its own loop variable (wifi.c:1464).

Save the three fields before the enrichment and re-assert them after, rather
than reverting 937 or making get_ctrl_interface_band() band-aware. The MediaTek
producer solves the identical problem the identical way, re-asserting
mlo_link_id after its own enrichment call (modules/mediatek/mtk.c:1570); that
module is not compiled for this target, but it is the in-tree precedent for
this hardware. Making get_ctrl_interface_band() resolve a per-link hostapd
socket the way qualcomm does (modules/qualcomm/qca.c:146, "%s_link%u") would be
the deeper fix - the sockets do exist here, ap-mld-1_link0..2 - but that helper
is shared by many callers and the blast radius is not worth it for this.

What this unblocks: map-agent reads mlo_links[].link_bssid to match a client to
an affiliated AP (bss_stations_data_cb). With every entry carrying link 0, the
match lands on one link twice, mld->stamldlist stays empty and the Associated
STA MLD Configuration Report TLV is never generated - so sta_mld and
affiliated_sta stay empty on the controller.

diff -urN a/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c b/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
--- a/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c	2026-08-02 12:18:46.045133343 +0200
+++ b/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c	2026-08-02 12:18:46.054096625 +0200
@@ -1945,10 +1945,28 @@
 		for (int j = 0; j < num_aplinks; j++) {
 			if (mlsta->sta[i].mlo_link_id == aplinks[j].id) {
 				struct wifi_sta *sta;
+				uint8_t link_macaddr[6];
+				uint8_t link_bssid[6];
+				uint8_t link_id;
 
 				sta = &mlsta->sta[i];
 				memcpy(sta->bssid, aplinks[j].macaddr, 6);
 
+				/* Keep the per-link identity across the enrichment
+				 * below. iface_get_sta_info_band() is handed the MLD
+				 * netdev and the MLD address of the client, and has no
+				 * per-link concept - get_ctrl_interface_band() drops
+				 * the band and returns the MLD ifname - so every link
+				 * queries the same hostapd socket and comes back with
+				 * mlo_link_id = 255 and the MLD addresses. Since 937
+				 * that enrichment is unconditional, so it now lands on
+				 * every link, not only where nl80211 had failed.
+				 * Re-asserting afterwards is what the MediaTek producer
+				 * does for the same reason (mtk.c:1570). */
+				link_id = sta->mlo_link_id;
+				memcpy(link_macaddr, sta->macaddr, 6);
+				memcpy(link_bssid, sta->bssid, 6);
+
 				ret = iface_get_sta_info_band(ifname, aplinks[j].band, macaddr, sta);
 				if (ret) {
 					/* Hostapd band enrichment can fail for a link the
@@ -1960,6 +1978,11 @@
 					break;
 				}
 
+				sta->mlo_link_id = link_id;
+				memcpy(sta->macaddr, link_macaddr, 6);
+				memcpy(sta->bssid, link_bssid, 6);
+				sta->mlo_capable = true;
+
 				if (!(sta->caps.valid & WIFI_CAP_EHT_VALID))
 					mlsta->mlo_capable = false;
 
